# 12. AI Working Rules

When working on this project:

## Rule 1 — Understand Context First

Use this rule and the project documentation as context before making major implementation decisions.

## Rule 2 — Separate Proposed Features From Confirmed Requirements

A feature described as potential, proposed, optional, or future must not be treated as mandatory.

## Rule 3 — Do Not Invent Business Rules

Do not create financial, booking, cancellation, refund, or permission rules without confirmation.

## Rule 4 — Preserve Existing Decisions

Do not replace established project decisions without explaining the reason and tradeoffs.

## Rule 5 — Separate Product Decisions From Technical Decisions

A product requirement should not automatically dictate the technical implementation.

## Rule 6 — Prefer Reusable Architecture

Use reusable components, clear abstractions, and avoid duplicated logic.

## Rule 7 — Admin Dashboard Is an Operational Product

Focus on workflows, search, filters, tables, statuses, actions, details, and permissions.

## Rule 8 — Ask Before High-Impact Assumptions

When a missing decision can materially affect architecture, UX, data models, or business logic, identify the issue before proceeding.

## Rule 9 — Do Not Over-Engineer

Prefer the simplest architecture that satisfies the confirmed requirements.

## Rule 10 — Do Not Modify Unrelated Areas

When implementing a feature, avoid changing unrelated parts of the project unless necessary.

